{"success": true, "data": {"markdown": "CAD Designer\n\nAdvanced 1 · Georgetown, Texas, United States (Hybrid) · 2 months ago · 26 applicants\n\nHybrid Full-timeEntry level\n\n1,001-5,000 employees · Utilities\n\nSee how you compare to 26 applicants. Try Premium for $0\n\n[See how you compare to 51 applicants. Try Premium for $0](https://www.linkedin.com/premium/products/?upsellOrderOrigin=member_jobs_jd_premium_banner&destRedirectURL=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Fjobs%2Fview%2Fcad-designer-at-advanced-1-4184654778%3F)\n\nApply\n\n[Apply](https://jobs.lever.co/advanced1/6fad92e4-fb4a-4f43-a2be-9b39be30a399)\n\nSave\n\nSave CAD Designer at Advanced 1\n\nShow more options\n\n[Show more options](#)\n\n## About the job\n\nAbout Advanced 1:\n\nAdvanced 1 is a leader in OSP engineering and design, providing top-tier engineering solutions to ISPs and major telecommunications operators. Our offerings include a full suite of services: OSP Engineering and Design, Fiber Splicing, Project Management, GIS Data Collection, and Construction Management. We're dedicated to building tomorrow's communities by delivering innovative, reliable, and cost-effective infrastructure solutions. Join our mission-driven team and help connect rural and urban communities to the broadband of tomorrow.\n\nJob Description:\n\nAdvanced 1 is seeking a skilled CAD Designer to join our engineering team. In this role, you will be responsible for producing precise, high-quality construction drawings, specifications, and technical documentation for fiber optic infrastructure projects. You will collaborate with our OSP engineers and GIS team to translate designs into detailed CAD drawings that guide construction and installation teams.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n* Produce high-quality fiber optic construction drawings and schematics using AutoCAD.\n\n* Translate GIS data and OSP engineering designs into detailed CAD drawings.\n\n* Collaborate with OSP engineers and GIS team members to ensure design accuracy.\n\n* Develop splice schematics, conduit layouts, aerial and underground designs\n\n* Develop splice schematics, conduit layouts, aerial and underground designs.\n\n* Conduct QC reviews of CAD drawings for compliance with project specifications and standards.\n\n* Maintain and update CAD files in an organized drawing management system.\n\n* Support permitting and regulatory submissions by preparing required technical documents.\n\n* Assist in the development and improvement of standard CAD templates and design standards.\n\n* Communicate with project teams to resolve design issues and implement revisions.\n\nQualifications:\n\n* Minimum 2 years of experience in CAD drafting, preferably in the telecommunications or utilities industry.\n\n* Proficiency in AutoCAD is required.\n\n* Experience with GIS tools such as ArcGIS, Katapult Pro, or similar platforms.\n\n* Knowledge of OSP fiber optic design principles.\n\n* Familiarity with fiber optic network components and construction methods.\n\n* Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings, specifications, and technical documents.\n\n* Attention to detail and commitment to accuracy in all design work.\n\n* Strong communication skills and ability to work in a collaborative team environment.\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n* Experience with telecommunications permitting processes and regulatory requirements.\n\n* Knowledge of make-ready engineering practices.\n\nSalary and Benefits:\n\n* Compensation will be commensurate with experience.\n\n* Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance\n\n* 401k Matching\n\n* Paid Time Off\n\nAdvanced 1 is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.\n\n## Similar jobs\n\n[CAD Designer\n\nAdvanced 1\n\n·\n\nGeorgetown, Texas, United States](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/cad-designer-at-advanced-1-4230399225?refId=Wz2Oze5lhEXyL53jC%2FjyOg%3D%3D&trackingId=GCcQ4c5%2FMv0i%3D&position=1&pageNum=0&trk=pub