...\n\n## About the job\n\nAbout Advanced 1:\n\nAdvanced 1 is in a significant growth phase, actively expanding our team to meet the demands of a rapidly growing market. We are looking for an experienced Senior OSP Engineer to join our team and take a leadership role in designing complex fiber optic networks. As a Senior OSP Engineer, you will lead projects from inception to completion, working with clients and internal teams to deliver top-tier fiber optic designs.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n* Lead and manage fiber optic network design projects.\n\n* Perform make-ready engineering and attachment analysis.\n\n* Design aerial and underground fiber optic networks using Katapult Pro and AutoCAD.\n\n* Collaborate with GIS, CAD, and project management teams.\n\n* Mentor junior engineers and designers.\n\n* Ensure compliance with industry standards, client specifications, and safety regulations.\n\n* Conduct field surveys and site assessments.\n\n* Prepare and review technical documentation, including specifications, cost estimates, and reports.\n\n* Assist in managing client relationships and ensuring project satisfaction.\n\nQualifications:\n\n* 5+ years of experience in OSP engineering, specifically in fiber optic network design.\n\n* Expert-level proficiency in Katapult Pro required.\n\n* Strong proficiency in AutoCAD.\n\n* Experience with GIS tools (ArcGIS, QGIS).\n\n* In-depth knowledge of NESC and local utility standards.\n\n* Knowledge of make-ready engineering, aerial construction, and underground installation techniques.\n\n* Strong leadership and project management skills.\n\n* Excellent communication and client interaction skills.\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n* PE license (or working towards).\n\n* Experience with BEAD or other federal broadband funding programs.\n\n* Familiarity with FCC regulations and broadband grant compliance.\n\n* Experience with RDOF, USDA ReConnect, or other federal/state funding programs.\